# Copy to .env.local and fill in. .env.local is gitignored.

# --- Auth (Better Auth) ----------------------------------------------------
# Base URL the app is served from in local dev.
BETTER_AUTH_URL=http://localhost:3000
# Any random 32-byte string: openssl rand -base64 32
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=

# DEMO ONLY. Sign-in also accepts this one fixed OTP, because no transactional email
# provider is wired up and a real code is therefore never delivered.
#
# Unset = off, and nothing special-cases the value anywhere. While it IS set, anyone
# holding the agent key can sign in as any email address and read that shopper's
# wishlist and order history — keep real data out of such a deployment. This is
# deliberately its own variable rather than a NODE_ENV or build-flag check, so turning
# it off is one visible change in one place.
#
# It changes only which code is accepted: account creation, response shapes and the
# uniform send/verify responses are identical either way.
# DEMO_OTP_CODE=000000

# --- Public site origin ----------------------------------------------------
# Origin the catalogue API builds its absolute `url` fields on — product links and
# collection links that an AI agent copies verbatim into a chat card.
#
# Must be https. An http value is upgraded with a warning, since the field is
# https-only. Unset falls back to VERCEL_PROJECT_PRODUCTION_URL and then to the
# production origin baked into lib/api/url.ts — never a relative path, which the
# consumer cannot resolve.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* is inlined at build time, so changing it needs a redeploy.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://shein-clone-ruby.vercel.app

# --- Test-only: name the shopper with a header ------------------------------
# DEMO ONLY. Lets X-Shopper-Email identify the shopper on every shopper-scoped route,
# instead of a bearer token. Unset = the header is not read at all and those routes
# need a token, as before.
#
# WHY IT EXISTS: the Instagram agent runtime cannot currently carry a bearer token
# between calls — no injection hook, and a new session per tool call — so the email-OTP
# token, which is the correct mechanism and is still implemented, is unusable there.
#
# WHAT IT COSTS: the caller asserts the address, so anyone holding AGENT_API_KEY can
# read or modify ANY shopper's bag, wishlist, profile and order history by naming their
# email. This is the same weakness X-Customer-Ref was removed for. Acceptable only
# because this deployment holds mock products and simulated payments. Turn it off and
# go back to tokens once the runtime supports them.
# ALLOW_SHOPPER_EMAIL_HEADER=1

# --- Test-only: delete a shopper -------------------------------------------
# DEMO ONLY. Enables DELETE /api/admin/users?email=..., which erases an account and
# everything it owns so a test address can be reused. Unset = the route answers 404,
# indistinguishable from one that does not exist.
#
# It needs DEMO_OTP_CODE set as well, and the caller must send that value as an
# X-Admin-Otp header on top of X-Agent-Key. So a deployment with a real mail provider
# and no fixed code has no delete endpoint at all.
#
# Be clear about the limits: X-Admin-Otp is the same short code the sign-in flow
# accepts, so it guards against a careless call, not against anyone holding the agent
# key. The endpoint also reports whether an address has an account, which the rest of
# this API deliberately avoids. Keep it off outside a demo.
# ALLOW_USER_DELETE=1

# --- Agent REST API --------------------------------------------------------
# Shared secret the Meta integration sends as X-Agent-Key on every request. Takes a
# comma-separated list so keys can be rotated without downtime. Unset = agent routes,
# including the OTP sign-in endpoints, are disabled and return 401. Outside production
# the well-known key `dev-agent-key` is accepted when this is unset; in production there
# is no fallback.
AGENT_API_KEY=

# --- Database (Postgres) ---------------------------------------------------
# Required by lib/db/index.ts for Better Auth, wishlist, and orders.
# Local PGlite server (npm run db): postgresql://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:5432/postgres
DATABASE_URL=

# --- Shopify Storefront API ------------------------------------------------
# Required by lib/shopify/client.ts for all product, collection, and search pages.
SHOPIFY_STORE_DOMAIN=your-store.myshopify.com
SHOPIFY_STOREFRONT_ACCESS_TOKEN=
